cff-version: "1.2.0"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "turtlend: Orthonormal-Frame Turtles in 3 and N Dimensions"
abstract: >
  turtlend provides TurtleND, a turtle that carries a position and an
  orthonormal frame through N-dimensional space. It moves along its heading,
  rotates by Givens rotations in the plane of any two basis vectors, converts
  points between global and turtle-local coordinates, and can add a dimension
  to a live frame without rebuilding it. The package also provides Turtle3D,
  the three-dimensional turtle that TurtleND generalizes, which builds
  molecular geometry from bond lengths, bond angles and dihedral angles, and
  the Vector3D class it is built on.
